<title>USA: RG&amp;E 470 MW Ginna nuke preparing startup.</title>
<headline>RG&amp;E 470 MW Ginna nuke preparing startup.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rochester Gas and Electric Corp's 470 megawatt Ginna nuclear power plant was making preparations to restart Tuesday following a shutdown for repairs, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said.</p>
<p>The Ontario, N.Y. plant was in &quot;hot standby&quot; mode and was &quot;making preparations for startup&quot; as of early Tuesday, the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>The Ginna plant was shut October 24 for tests after impurities were discovered in the oil that cools the plant's transformer.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
</text>
